---

## 📊 Data Preprocessing

Before training the model, the historical stock data is prepared through several steps:

1. Load the historical stock dataset.
2. Select the relevant price features.
3. Handle missing or inconsistent values.
4. Normalize the data.
5. Create sequences using previous time steps.
6. Divide the dataset into training and testing sets.

Normalization helps the neural network train more effectively by keeping numerical values within a suitable range.

---

## 🧩 LSTM Model

The model uses an LSTM architecture to process historical sequences.

A typical architecture can be represented as:

```text
Input Time-Series Data
        ↓
LSTM Layer
        ↓
LSTM Layer
        ↓
Dense Layer
        ↓
Predicted Stock Price
```

The model is trained by minimizing the difference between the predicted and actual stock prices.

